# Club, district, and account-access agents

Causey has two institutional buyers. Load the matching skill before changing org/portal UX. Load the access skill before changing roles, People invites, claim, Account settings, or permission gates.

## Club / team owner
Skill: `.cursor/skills/club-owner-readiness/SKILL.md`  
Backlog: `.cursor/club-readiness.md`  
Walk roster → travel/host → attendance → **results** → season report. Copy says Club/Team, never School/District. Do not build pairings, dues, DMs, or a public club directory.

## School district
Skill: `.cursor/skills/district-program-readiness/SKILL.md`  
Backlog: `.cursor/district-readiness.md`  
Walk provision schools → handoff → **school and district tournaments** → family RSVP → aggregate reports. Copy says School/District. No self-serve district signup, no partner names, fail-closed reports.

## Account-access customizability
Skill: `.cursor/skills/account-access-customizability/SKILL.md`  
Backlog: `.cursor/account-access-readiness.md`  
For **every workflow**, one named agent walks **each account type**: settings they should have, missing features, and whether access can be granted **only** to the right role and scope (named roles + group assignment, not Salesforce ACLs). Person accounts stay student / parent / coach.

## Shared
Playbook: `.cursor/club-district-perfection-loop.md`. One workflow win per tick. `dev` only; never `main`. Update the matching backlog + `.cursor/district-ux-progress.md`.
